WEBVTT

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:20.100
What do you think, Anne?

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.430
Won't my heroic figure impress her?

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.360
What do you like about Duke Richard?

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.150
Good question.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:37.910
I like how strong-willed she is,
and she has a charming face as well.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.370
But you're enemies.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:43.330
Enemy or not, she can
be mine if I become king.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:47.080
Also, she never pays attention to me.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.540
I like that about her.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.920
Do you, um...

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.970
Do you resent your father for
things turning out this way?

00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:00.510
I don't resent him.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.100
This is all fate, dictated by God.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.270
God, God, God!

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:13.400
Don't put your trust in God!
To hell with any fate decided for you!

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:16.950
Take what you want with your own strength!

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.820
You can't have Richard, though.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.620
That's a surprise, coming from you.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.040
Why do you laugh?

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.130
But women are best when
they're cheerful. That's for certain.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.800
Edward.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.970
We may not be able to love each other,
but I'm sure we can be friends.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:40.850
Friends...

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:45.930
Say, would you mind playing chess with me?

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.140
I'm really hopeless at embroidery.

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.730
York of the white rose.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:56.360
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:02.780
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:07.500
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.430
The mist has thickened.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.440
This is the end.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:59.400
I <i>will </i>avenge father's death
on Lancaster in this battle!

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.110
King Edward!

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:11.040
Not so much as a flourish
of trumpets. What an insult!

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:14.420
Warwick.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.500
It appears you've lost your way.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.090
You're the one who's lost.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:24.930
Do you intend to challenge us
with such a paltry force?

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.720
You don't know how to treat ambassadors,

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.810
you aren't content with one woman,

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:32.980
and you can't even contrive
to defend yourself!

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.600
How can a man like you shoulder
the burden of a kingdom?!

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:40.690
Even your own brother forsook you!

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:42.940
Look, Edward.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:49.700
The brother who abandoned you has come,
leading an army to rival your own!

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.410
You're late. Did Margaret's
forces arrive in time?

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:09.800
Did you think my brother
cold enough to turn his blade

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:12.520
against his own blood and rightful king?

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.310
Hear me, Warwick!

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:18.940
I've repented my infidelity,
and to regain my brother's trust,

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:22.530
I hereby denounce you as my mortal foe!

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:24.940
Now our forces are evenly matched!

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:28.780
I'll return the wound you gave
my heart a hundred-fold!

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.660
You'll pay for this.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.290
Traitor!

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:40.710
If Henry made good his escape
from London, he could be in that army.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.880
Charge!

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.720
How are we supposed to fight in this mist?

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.810
Follow me!

00:05:54.890 --> 00:06:00.270
I can see! I can see the
red blood of Lancaster!

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:08.450
Your Majesty, until the battle is decided,

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:13.740
I suggest you remain concealed
away from Warwick's host.

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.830
O Lord.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:20.330
May victory favor whoever you will.

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:24.460
No. I don't wish for
anyone to come to harm.

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.420
Not a soul.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.300
Your Majesty!

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.550
I...

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:34.060
I've always believed that
my heart was with my people.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:40.060
But I kept averting my gaze from reality--
from everyone's pain.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:44.070
I must witness it with my
own eyes, close at hand.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.070
As king, I must see its end.

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.120
Duke Richard!

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:01.580
In this mist, we risk...

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.670
Richard!

00:07:03.670 --> 00:07:07.050
If we attack each other
by mistake in this mist,

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:09.920
fear and suspicion could lead to a rout.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.350
Buckingham.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:17.310
You'll halt the soldiers
here as "Richard."

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.390
What?!

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:22.810
Listen. From now on, this man is me.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:24.110
Assist the duke.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.190
Y-Yes, sir!

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.730
Wait, Richard!

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.110
Are you going to charge in alone?

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:32.410
Not alone. I'll have comrades.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.570
What comrades?

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:38.700
Our forces are evenly matched,

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:43.290
but they'll be reinforced
if the battle drags on.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:47.170
Edward, I'll join the battle
alongside Richard and his men.

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:50.920
George, if you slay Warwick,
Isabelle will never...

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:52.010
But...

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.680
Remain at my side.
I'll strike down Warwick.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:03.850
We just need some blow to turn the tide.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.650
Warwick's banner.

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:12.070
The main Lancastrian force
must be that way.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:23.250
You there.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.460
Follow me!

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:29.090
There's the enemy line!
They haven't noticed us in the mist!

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:31.050
We can take them by surprise!

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:35.010
I'm off to win glory!
Any cowards can stay here!

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.300
--Wait for me!
--Let's go!

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.260
I'll join you!

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.560
Don't miss this opportunity!

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:42.520
Follow me, Lancastrian soldiers.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:47.690
Allies?

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.230
Slay the foe!

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.950
Shatter Lancaster!

00:08:56.950 --> 00:08:58.370
My lord earl!

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:01.450
The rear of our main line
has suddenly collapsed!

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:04.120
What?! Has the enemy been reinforced?!

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:09.170
No, my lord. It seems that...
our own men are fighting each other.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.760
They're fighting each other?
That's pleasant news.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:17.140
I knew that heaven was on our side!

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:19.930
Gentlemen! Victory is within our grasp!

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:23.180
Let us crush them in a single blow!

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.480
Advance!

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.020
Charge!

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:34.690
This infernal mist!

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:48.630
Impossible.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:49.880
Warwick!

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:53.300
Did you not swear to make me king?!

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:55.800
No. No.

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.010
You must understand, I...

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:00.640
You defiled my spirit!

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:04.180
No, I gave you everything.

00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:06.140
I gave it all to make you king!

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:09.310
Yes! I am your king!

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:12.360
Warwick!

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.030
Edward!

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:18.490
How I loathe your face.

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:21.410
It's you who defiled your father's spirit!

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:22.490
Edward!

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:26.330
Don't interfere! This man's life is mine!

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.960
A duel between us?

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:34.630
Have you forgotten that I taught
you swordsmanship as a child?

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:43.300
The sun will set soon, Edward.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:46.100
I knew that you were strong, Warwick.

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.890
I can't let you defeat me yet.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:54.860
Still, you have talent.
Perhaps it runs in your blood.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:57.240
He'll soon surpass me.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:04.910
Warwick.

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:09.580
If I fall in the course of our endeavor,

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:13.500
please, place Edward on the throne.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.760
Swear it to me.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:21.840
Swear that York will have the crown.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:30.640
Now!

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:32.520
Warwick!

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:37.980
My lord! Please escape!

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:40.700
Our army will collapse if this goes on!

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.990
We should fall back and regroup!

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:45.700
He fled! Pursue him!

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:46.790
Wait!

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:50.620
You must... You must take him alive.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.170
Do not kill him.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:54.540
Damn!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.800
I refuse to let this be the end!

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:00.090
I've bent all of England to my will!

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:04.760
If we join with Margaret's army,
we can fight again at once!

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.600
The crown...

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.270
The crown is still in my hands!

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:26.120
Warwick, your time is over.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:28.280
From now on, I am...

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:30.540
...the kingmaker.

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:33.790
Warwick!

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.290
Who struck him?!

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:37.880
Seize and behead his killer at once!

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:42.880
Warwick. Oh, my sorrowful shadow.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:46.180
If you die, my darkness dies with you.

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:51.100
A-Are you there?

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:55.100
Is someone...?

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:58.310
So, Death has veiled your eyes.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:01.530
Don't you recognize your mortal foe?

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:03.110
It's strange.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:07.030
Now that I know I'll lose you,
I remember only the beautiful times.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:13.000
Oh, so even glory is worthless now.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:19.710
My hands are empty, and my body
will soon sink into the earth.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:23.670
Nothing remains to me.

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:29.970
Long live His Majesty!

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:33.390
Look. The young new king is here.

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:42.730
How dignified and handsome he is.

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:47.740
Father, is that King Henry VI?

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:51.910
Why, that's Richard Plantagenet,
Duke of York.

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:54.080
King Henry is over there.

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:00.960
That's the king?

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:04.510
The Duke of York looks
far statelier and more regal.

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:11.550
Oh, how beautiful would he look

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.850
with a crown upon his head?

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:30.410
I will hold back your departing soul.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.080
Do not die by any hand but mine.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:38.040
I am your king.

00:14:39.120 --> 00:14:41.750
My...

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.750
My king?

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.010
Your Majesty.

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:52.430
Let us meet again... before the Lord God.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:03.770
What's wrong?

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:06.360
You can follow us in a carriage, you know.

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:11.570
I'll be fine. I'm anxious to
find out how the war is going.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:13.660
The outcome is obvious.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:18.750
By the time we arrive, your father
will be toasting our victory

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.500
with a goblet of Yorkist blood.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:25.800
Father would never harm the House of York!

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:30.470
He's really the most
compassionate person there is.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:35.430
Oh, I don't think that Warwick
will kill the York brothers.

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:38.480
He's a reasonable man at heart.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:40.940
I'm sorry.

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:44.190
But I'm frightened.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:51.860
I feel like this battle will change
my heart, no matter what happens.

00:15:53.370 --> 00:15:54.740
Rest easy.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:16:01.500
Whatever happens, you'll still be my wife.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:06.460
I'm not like my father!
I'm a man who protects his family!

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:10.590
So, just pray for a
Lancastrian victory for now.

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:13.090
You're a member of the House of Lancaster.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:18.140
You're right. I'm not a Neville anymore.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:22.980
From now on, I'll defend the royal
family as a Lancastrian noblewoman.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:27.980
A Yorkist is fleeing! Give chase!

00:16:27.980 --> 00:16:30.440
No! I'm not with York!

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:35.910
H-Help! I'm...

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:37.080
Don't worry.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:46.500
I'm your king.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.590
You're the king?

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:54.590
My subject, your suffering is my own.

00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:58.050
But all that I can do is pray.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:02.640
A-Are you really the king?
I don't believe it.

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:05.690
You look like a young man.

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:08.190
I've come to weep like you do.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:12.240
You and I are the same.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:17.740
You're lying.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:20.910
If you really are the king,

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:25.670
your brow should be wrinkled
with long years of suffering.

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:28.460
Your skin should be stained
with blood and dirt.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:31.380
You could never keep yourself so clean!

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:36.720
We ended up covered in blood
because our king refused to be!

00:17:36.720 --> 00:17:40.310
It's all your fault!
I'm going to die because of you!

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:42.720
I'll die without even
knowing what life is--

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.270
Who are you?

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:50.820
Are you a Lancastrian?!
A Yorkist?! Tell me, or I'll kill you!

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:53.570
Why did you...?

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:55.900
He was a Lancastrian.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.370
What? That can't be!

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:02.910
O Lord.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:06.210
It's not my fault!
A nobleman ordered me to do it!

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:10.290
On the battlefield, killing is the only
choice, whoever we fight for!

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:12.090
We must kill!

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:14.340
We do it to live!

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:15.380
Your Majesty!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:19.550
Did I imagine it?

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:22.510
No. I'm sure I heard it.

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:25.480
Where is he? King Henry is here somewhere!

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:32.110
Over here, Richard.

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:34.280
Henry is that way.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:37.490
Do you expect me to believe you?

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:38.780
Don't interfere.

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.370
It's true. I'm not lying.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:46.160
Now, come on.
Your beloved Henry is waiting.

00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:49.290
Hm? That's not right.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:52.000
It's King Henry who's waiting for you.

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:56.380
Oh, no. Your beloved Henry
is waiting for you too.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.800
Come, Richard.

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:02.850
Come this way if you want to see Henry.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:06.810
Wait, Richard.

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:09.020
Don't listen to the witch.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:12.810
That woman means only to deceive you.

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:15.230
The king is beyond that thicket.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:20.240
If you follow the witch, you'll never
be able to slay Henry again.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:22.870
Avenge me.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:25.160
Secure the throne for York!

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:29.870
Richard, come with me
if you want to see Henry.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:32.880
Richard, trust me.

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:34.790
Trust only my words.

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:36.630
Do it to kill Henry!

00:19:36.630 --> 00:19:38.550
Come, Richard!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.680
Joan.

00:19:42.720 --> 00:19:43.800
Richard.

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:45.510
Begone, fiend!

00:19:47.350 --> 00:19:48.640
Richard.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:53.480
But I'm the only one

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:55.230
who knows the real you.

00:19:56.440 --> 00:20:01.150
Father, I will avenge you
with my own hands.

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:03.780
Swear it, Richard.

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.490
Like you did then.

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:10.330
Please guide me, Father.

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:13.790
Lead me to King Henry!

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:18.510
Please escape while you
still can, Your Majesty!

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.880
Why did this man die?

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:25.050
Or that boy?

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:29.350
Neither of them would
have died if not for me.

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:31.770
It's my fault.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:34.980
Wait for me. Once I've slain the king,

00:20:34.980 --> 00:20:38.780
I'll go to our forest, Henry.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:41.900
It's you yourself that I like.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:46.530
That's right. No matter who
you are, you're my...

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:48.910
What is it?

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:52.830
Unless my eyes deceive me,
I saw King Henry!

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:54.370
He was over that way.

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:55.630
Did you say Henry?

00:21:00.170 --> 00:21:01.420
Duke Richard!

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:07.680
I killed them.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.680
I've been killing them.

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:13.810
Let's flee, Your Majesty!

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:16.190
Names and titles don't matter.

00:21:16.190 --> 00:21:19.230
Henry, you are my light.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:23.780
So, I'm going to kill the king...

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:32.330
...and gain light.

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:42.920
Henry.

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:46.130
Richard.

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:51.470
Who are you?

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:53.100
My...

00:21:53.100 --> 00:21:56.140
My name is Richard.

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:59.060
Richard Plantagenet.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:05.490
Son of the Duke of York,
whom the Lancastrians murdered.

00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:11.330
Henry... who are you?

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:15.460
I am...

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:20.250
I am the King of England.
